      "instruction": "For each question, choose the correct answer.",
      "material": [
        {
          "id": "h5",
          "type": "heading",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "A fantastic business idea"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "id": "i7",
          "type": "imageRef",
          "image": "img7"
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "When sisters Caroline and Isabel Bercaw were 11 and 12 years old, bath bombs (coloured balls that you add to your bath water to make it smell nice) suddenly became very popular. Caroline and Isabel often used them, especially after doing sports, and so did their friends. They all thought that the bath bombs made bath-time feel special."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Caroline and Isabel got so interested in bath bombs that they looked online and found some instructions for how to make their own. Their first ones weren’t great, but they practised until their bath bombs were perfect. Then they had the clever idea of adding a surprise in the centre of each one, such as a small toy or a piece of jewellery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "When they had a big box of their new bath bombs, they agreed on a price, and then took them to a local market to find out if people wanted to buy them. The girls couldn’t believe it when they sold all the bombs in just a few hours."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "After that, they began to work hard on their business. They had a lot to learn, and asked for help whenever they needed it. They spoke to their teachers at school, called business owners, and of course talked to their parents. Soon, they were selling their bath bombs in shops all over their home town."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The business continued to grow and is now a big success. The girls think this is because of the little gift inside each bath bomb. This made their bombs exciting and fun to use, especially for young people."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
